---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Updates from '../components/Updates.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import {faqs,emailLink} from '../data/festival';
---
<Layout title="Plan Your Visit | Breck Sky Fest" description="Plan for Breck Sky Fest with family information, clothing advice, ticket status, accessibility, weather, and official Breckenridge travel resources. Dates and venues TBA.">
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Your festival field guide" title="Pack your curiosity. And a warm coat." description="A little preparation makes a mountain evening much more enjoyable. Here’s what we know now, and what’s still coming." icon="mountain" accent="blue"/>
  <section class="section paper-section" id="dates"><div class="wrap"><div class="planning-grid"><div class="planning-card"><Icon name="clock" size={30}/><span class="eyebrow">When</span><h2>November 2026</h2><p>Planned month. Exact dates and event times are TBA.</p></div><div class="planning-card"><Icon name="pin" size={30}/><span class="eyebrow">Where</span><h2>Breckenridge, CO</h2><p>Venues, street addresses, and the festival map are coming soon.</p></div><div class="planning-card"><Icon name="ticket" size={30}/><span class="eyebrow">Tickets</span><h2>Coming soon</h2><p>Free community activities and a ticketed signature event are planned.</p></div></div><div class="notice"><Icon name="clock" size={26}/><div><strong>Before you book your trip</strong><p>Wait for confirmed festival dates and venues before making travel arrangements specifically for Breck Sky Fest. Registration, prices, and cancellation terms will be available before ticket sales open.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section paper-section visit-prep"><div class="wrap feature-split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Family planning</span><h2>Make room for<br/>small discoveries.</h2><p>Daytime science and community telescope viewing are at the heart of the family program. You can choose activities that suit your children’s ages, attention spans, and bedtime once the schedule is announced.</p><ul class="check-list"><li><Icon name="stars" size={18}/>Children stay with their accompanying adult.</li><li><Icon name="stars" size={18}/>Age guidance and session lengths will be listed per event.</li><li><Icon name="stars" size={18}/>Toilets, seating, food, and warm-up spaces are still to be confirmed.</li><li><Icon name="stars" size={18}/>No telescope or astronomy background needed for the main observing sessions.</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/program/">Browse the program preview <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div><div class="packing-card"><span class="eyebrow">A November night’s packing list</span><h3>Warm from<br/>head to toe.</h3><ul><li>Warm coat and insulating layers</li><li>Hat, gloves, and warm socks</li><li>Sturdy footwear for possible snow or ice</li><li>A thermos, water, and a snack</li><li>Hand warmers, if you have them</li><li>A dim red light for observing sessions</li></ul><p>Standing still gets chilly. Plan for breaks, and keep bright phone screens and flashlights away from telescope viewing areas.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Getting here & getting around</span><h2>A good weekend<br/>starts with a little planning.</h2></div><p class="section-aside">Event-specific directions, parking, drop-off points, and any festival transport will appear with confirmed venues.</p></div><div class="resource-grid"><a href="https://gobreck.com/" class="resource-card"><span>Official visitor guide</span><h3>Explore Breckenridge</h3><p>Find places to stay, things to do, and town travel information.</p><Icon name="diagonal" size={26}/></a><a href="https://www.breckfreeride.com/" class="resource-card"><span>Local public transport</span><h3>Breck Free Ride</h3><p>Check current routes and operating times. Festival connections are TBA.</p><Icon name="diagonal" size={26}/></a><a href="https://www.cotrip.org/" class="resource-card"><span>Before you drive</span><h3>Colorado road conditions</h3><p>Check current road conditions and travel alerts with COtrip.</p><Icon name="diagonal" size={26}/></a></div><p class="small light-note">These are general visitor resources. Festival lodging offers, shuttles, and mountain access are not yet confirmed.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section paper-section" id="accessibility"><div class="wrap info-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Access & comfort</span><h2>Let’s plan for<br/>your visit.</h2><p>We’re still selecting venues. We will publish step-free access, path surfaces, seating, toilets, telescope access, and any relevant sensory information for each event.</p><p>If there is something that would help you or your family take part, tell us while we are planning.</p><a class="text-link" href={emailLink('Access question')}>Ask an access question <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div><div><span class="eyebrow">Weather & changes</span><h2>The sky has<br/>a say, too.</h2><p>Clouds affect telescope viewing, and snow or wind can affect outdoor plans. We will publish each event’s weather arrangements and any alternatives before registration opens.</p><p>Refund terms, change notices, and where to check on the day will be included with confirmed ticketed events.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Contact the festival <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section paper-section faq-preview" id="questions"><div class="wrap faq-split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Good to know</span><h2>Your questions,<br/>answered.</h2><p>Something else on your mind?</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Ask us <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div><div class="faq-list">{faqs.map(faq=><details><summary>{faq.q}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{faq.a}</p></details>)}</div></div></section>
  <Updates/>
</Layout>
